{
  "_README": "EXAMPLE ONLY — this file is NOT active. Claude Code reads .claude/settings.json (strict JSON, no comments). To turn the answer_key guardrail ON, copy the block below into .claude/settings.json (create it if needed) or your ~/.claude/settings.json. Leaving this as .example keeps it inactive.",
  "_what_this_does": "Blocks Claude Code's file tools (Read/Grep/Glob, and read-only Bash like cat/head) from opening models/answer_key/, and blocks edits (Edit/Write) to it — so an AI assistant won't peek at or copy the lab reference solutions. NOTE: this governs Claude Code only; it does NOT affect dbt Wizard in the dbt platform. It also won't stop a custom subprocess (e.g. a python script) that opens files itself.",
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Read(models/answer_key/**)",
      "Edit(models/answer_key/**)"
    ]
  }
}
